From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:45:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 603/604] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: do not hold the
 I2C buses for VBUS

Until a client's driver binds, fw_devlink counts the client's suppliers
against its parent. The two Type-C controllers name VBUS regulators that
are only available later: the right port's GPIO regulator is a module
that nothing loads, and the left port's is the charger's boost on the
other bus. Both I2C0 and I2C1 then deferred for good on station boot
c85e7cb8, and the charger and its guard on I2C0 never bound.

Mark both regulators post-init providers. The Type-C driver still waits
for its VBUS regulator itself.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts      | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index 353d0b05e..abe9d1775 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -726,6 +726,8 @@ typec@25 {
 		compatible = "onsemi,fusb301";
 		reg = <0x25>;
 		vbus-supply = <&usb0_vbus>;
+		/* See the right port's controller: the bus must not wait for it. */
+		post-init-providers = <&usb0_vbus>;
 
 		connector {
 			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
@@ -773,6 +775,13 @@ typec@25 {
 		interrupt-parent = <&pio>;
 		interrupts = <3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH>;
 		vbus-supply = <&usb1_vbus>;
+		/*
+		 * Until the controller's own driver binds, fw_devlink counts its
+		 * suppliers against the I2C adapter, and the regulator is a
+		 * module nothing loads: the whole bus, and the charger guard on
+		 * it, would wait forever. The driver asks for VBUS itself.
+		 */
+		post-init-providers = <&usb1_vbus>;
 
 		connector {
 			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
-- 
